Removes the lag of huge decks in Slay the Spire 2: thousands of cards, hundreds of relics, in singleplayer and in co-op.

[b]Playing with Limitless or BaseLib?[/b] The mod also speeds up a large part of their work during combat, with the same results.

[b]In co-op, every player needs this mod.[/b] The game won't let a player without it join.
Why: with a huge deck, the mod speeds the game up so much that a player without it falls far behind. For example, with about 8,000 cards and a few hundred relics, starting a combat takes about 4 seconds with the mod and over 30 seconds without it. The game can't handle players that far apart: the cards played in the meantime get lost, and the run desyncs or freezes.

[b]Want a settings menu?[/b] Install [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3737335127]BaseLib[/url] (optional) to turn each improvement on or off from the game's settings.

[b]Disclaimer:[/b] this mod is still in early development. I will update it regularly for a while, to spot any bug and optimize the game further.

Feedback will be highly appreciated! Don't hesitate to leave a comment ❤️

[h2]What it changes[/h2]
With a huge deck, the game slows down more and more until every action freezes it. With the mod:
[list]
[*][b]Entering a combat:[/b] with 8,000+ cards and hundreds of relics, about 4 seconds instead of half a minute.
[*][b]Playing cards:[/b] smooth again, even past 10,000 cards.
[*][b]Cards that search your piles:[/b] cards like Hidden Gem no longer freeze the game.
[*][b]Copying lots of cards:[/b] a campfire clone or Reflections' Shatter with thousands of cards takes seconds instead of minutes, and relics that trigger on every copy (Bing Bong) no longer black out the screen or crash the game.
[*][b]Waiting in combat:[/b] no more constant stutter.
[*][b]End of combat:[/b] no more long freeze before the rewards.
[*][b]Co-op:[/b] the long pause after every action is gone. Players with big decks no longer slow down everyone else.
[*][b]Deck view and card grids:[/b] sorting, opening and scrolling are fast again.
[*][b]Lots of relics:[/b] moving the mouse no longer slows the game down.
[*][b]Optional:[/b] the relic effects at the start of a combat skip their animation pauses. It looks faster, and the effects stay exactly the same. In solo you can make it start only from a number of relics (always on in co-op).
[/list]

[h2]What it doesn't change[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]The game itself:[/b] same rules, same results, same saves. The mod only makes the game do the same work faster.
[*][b]Your other mods:[/b] it needs no other mod and works alongside Limitless, BetterSpire2, CampfireTrade, ModConfig and Unlimited. If another mod changes the same part of the game, this mod steps aside there.
[*][b]Its safety:[/b] after a game or mod update, any part of the mod that no longer fits turns itself off instead of guessing.
[/list]
Co-op with very big decks is much better, but not instant: going from one turn to the next can still take a few seconds.

[h2]Why this mod exists[/h2]
Slay the Spire 2 isn't made for thousands of cards and hundreds of relics, but a run can get there:
[list]
[*][b]In vanilla:[/b] [b]Pael's Growth[/b] (start of act 2) lets you clone a card at every rest site, copies included, so their number doubles each time. Add [b]Bing Bong[/b], [b]Dolly's Mirror[/b] or the [b]Reflections[/b] event and a good run ends with thousands of cards.
[*][b]With other mods:[/b] many mods give you more cards and relics, or more time to collect them. [b]Limitless[/b], for example, adds infinite acts, so you can keep cloning forever.
[*][b]In co-op:[/b] the lag comes from the cards and relics of all players together. 4 players with 2,000 cards each lag about as much as one player with 8,000, so a laggy amount comes much sooner.
[/list]


[h2]Settings[/h2]
Everything is on by default. With [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3737335127]BaseLib[/url] (optional), each improvement has its own switch under [b]Mod Configuration → Big Deck Optimization[/b].

You can also use the console ([b]`[/b] key, [b]*[/b] or [b]^[/b] on AZERTY; without BaseLib, these changes last until you quit the game):
[list]
[*][b]bdopt[/b] shows what is on.
[*][b]bdopt off[/b] / [b]bdopt on[/b] turns the whole mod off or back on, without restarting.
[*][b]bdopt fast_combat_start off[/b] turns off just the faster combat start. In co-op it stays on for everyone, so all players start each combat at the same pace.
[/list]

Source code (MIT): https://github.com/TheKiwi7/big-deck-optimization

[h2]Something looks wrong?[/h2]
Check whether the bug still happens with the mod turned off, then switch it back on:
[list]
[*]With BaseLib: in [b]Mod Configuration → Big Deck Optimization[/b], untick [b]Optimizations enabled[/b].
[*]With or without BaseLib: open the console and type [b]bdopt off[/b] ([b]bdopt on[/b] to switch it back on).
[/list]
In co-op, every player turns it off (and back on) together, for the same reason: a player with the mod off falls far behind the others.

Then report it in the comments.
